WEBVTT

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:02.610
Here's my next request.

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:08.390
At 3 PM, go do some shopping in the
supermarket near Nanasaka Middle School.

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.610
<i>It's almost 3 PM.</i>

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.070
<b>SWEETS
CHOCOLATE</b>

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:22.470
Was Souma Sumire trying to make us meet her?

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:23.670
I don't know.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.580
I already said no!

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.380
I got a good score on my last test,
and you said you'd buy it then!

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.090
The test was last month!

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.260
The second incident should happen around now.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:49.270
Hey, Kei, it's been a while.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.060
It certainly has.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.020
I was actually just thinking
that I should contact you.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:55.070
I'll help you.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.400
But I want something in exchange.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:58.490
What is it?

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.410
A picture of Souma Sumire.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:03.450
Did Minami ask you for it?

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:05.540
You sure figure things out quickly.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:08.290
I thought it'd be easiest to ask you for it.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.210
Should you really be telling me about this?

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:13.170
It's not something I have to research in secret.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.960
I'm sure she's in the yearbook.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:19.470
That'll do. Take a picture with
your phone and send it to me.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:20.800
Can do that much.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.510
So? What do you want to know?

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:26.100
About the traffic accident
that happened this morning.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.850
Ah, it's indeed the kind of
case you'd get involved in.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.480
A case? Not an accident?

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.110
That's apparently what the Bureau's concluded.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:38.320
It's one of the serial ability rampage cases.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:43.490
Another one was everyone in a supermarket
suddenly bursting out laughing.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:48.080
How big of an issue is this case for the Bureau?

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.370
No idea.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:51.120
But something feels wrong.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.750
On the surface, it's not that big of a case.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:59.420
And yet, it seems to me they're panicking.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.760
If I had to be honest...

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:06.850
I'd say the Bureau fears the possibility
that all abilities could go berserk.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:18.270
<i>Two abilities went out of control.</i>

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:21.440
<i>The Witch disappeared from
Sakurada two months ago.</i>

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:25.030
<i>She didn't foresee the problem
just two months in the future.</i>

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:29.540
<i>What's worse,
something similar might happen again.</i>

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:32.040
<i>There are tens of thousands
of ability users in Sakurada.</i>

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:37.040
<i>That means there's a risk of all
of their abilities going berserk.</i>

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:41.550
<i>How will the Bureau deal with such a problem?</i>

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:50.260
<i>It was around forty years ago.</i>

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:57.480
<i>The one year between the first abilities
appearing and the Bureau being established.</i>

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:02.240
<b>Piano School
Urachi
<i>Back when only three people in
the world were aware of abilities...</i></b>

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:03.110
<i>Back when only three people in
the world were aware of abilities...</i>

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:11.740
If we execute this plan,
you'll meet a terrible fate without doubt.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:16.170
We three discussed many possibilities together.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:21.090
And I confirmed the futures behind all of our ideas.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:25.340
The fate this plan will lead to is the
lesser evil of all possible outcomes.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:29.220
There might be something you haven't checked.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:34.230
I'm sure there has to be a way to make
the whole world forget about abilities.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:37.940
We couldn't find a way to get rid of all abilities,

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:41.570
but we could create a world
where no one knows about them.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.030
With the help of my ability.

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:48.030
The ability to erase one specific piece
of information from the whole world.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:52.990
To make one memory disappear
from the heads of all people.

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:55.290
Actually, even at this very moment,

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:59.580
I'm making all people outside
of this room unaware of abilities.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:05.460
However, when the time comes for you to leave
this world, everyone will remember about them.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:09.090
The world will be overwhelmed by them,
and the chaos will be unimaginable.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:13.850
That's the future I've seen. I assure you,
it's a future that we cannot allow to happen.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:17.850
Which is why we need to protect your ability.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.100
Forever...

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:25.070
To achieve that, we have to let
other ability users be born.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:28.490
We'll have to expand the border
to cover at least all of Sakurada,

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.320
and keep those outside of it unaware of abilities.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:35.370
Your wife happens to have the perfect ability.

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:39.040
The ability to never lose a specific thing...

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:43.750
If she specifies this cup to never
be lost in regard to this room,

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:47.300
no one will be able to take this cup outside of it.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:52.010
If she specifies the warmth
to never be lost in regard to this tea,

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:54.390
it'll never go cold.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:57.060
She's using her ability in regard to this room,

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:01.190
to make sure we don't lose
our memories about abilities.

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:05.860
If you leave this room,
you'll forget all about abilities.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:09.780
We need to expand this border
to cover all of Sakurada.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:15.790
I'll keep watching the future with my ability
to predict any accidents related to abilities.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.540
Twenty years, was it?

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:19.500
Yes.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:22.710
In twenty years, one of Sakurada's residents

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:25.630
will get an ability that can stop your time.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:27.460
But it's twenty years

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:30.680
assuming that ability users
will be born in this town, right?

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:32.430
If we moved to another town,

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:35.430
it's possible the ability user
we need would be born sooner.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:38.310
And what good will speeding things up do?

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:41.390
You'll be able to live like a normal person.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:44.310
You'll forget about all abilities and live in peace.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:48.280
It'll take ten years for me to lose my name.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:51.780
I'll be able to stay human
for at least another ten years.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:54.370
I'm chronically ill.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:57.660
I'm not supposed to live more
than just two more years.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:01.830
In the future I saw,
if more abilities are born in Sakurada,

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:04.540
you'll be able to live for another twenty years.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:07.750
That seems very unfair.

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:10.590
You're supposed to be able to live normally,

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:14.300
and yet in just ten years,
you'll have to throw away even your own name.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:18.890
I'm sure the reason you got this ability

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:21.270
was to let your beloved forget about your death.

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:22.180
Who knows.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:26.440
But in truth, you don't want to be forgotten.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:32.030
That's why your ability
will lose its effect once you die.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:36.820
What an ironic contradiction.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:42.790
If Sakurada becomes the town of
ability users and you keep on living,

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:46.040
the two of you will eventually have a child, a boy.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:51.340
I think we should try our best for his sake as well.

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:56.390
<i>Then, a year passed,
and the Bureau had built its foundations.</i>

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:58.890
<i>The border was forcefully expanded.</i>

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:03.890
<i>Its new size was keeping
the whole of Sakurada in check.</i>

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:12.940
<i>Erasing this border and getting rid of all
memories of abilities all around the world</i>

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:16.240
<i>is definitely the Bureau's trump card.</i>

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.040
<i>A message from Hitsuuchi...</i>

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:24.540
<i>It's the info on the people
from the ability rampage cases.</i>

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:33.010
Hello? Asai here.

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:34.300
I know.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:37.130
You sent me the picture of Souma Sumire.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:38.930
Was it okay?

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:40.760
It reminded me of something.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:42.890
Tell me, what's going on?

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:43.930
What do you mean?

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:47.060
Just who is Souma Sumire?

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:51.070
She's a girl who passed away
two years ago in an accident.

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:53.230
I know that.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:55.780
But I also know it's not all.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:56.570
Why's that?

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.200
I've met her once.

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:01.160
<i>So that's what it was!</i>

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:04.580
When was it that you met her?

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:07.540
Two years ago. June, if I remember correctly.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:10.380
She suddenly appeared at my place.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.170
<i>So my hunch was right.</i>

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:15.380
<i>When he met Souma years ago,</i>

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:17.630
<i>she must have had him manipulate memories.</i>

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:20.890
Wasn't that when you were still a vampire?

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.720
That's right.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:26.520
Before the Bureau noticed me,
that girl was the only one

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:29.730
who knew about me absorbing
information from people.

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.310
In exchange for keeping the secret,

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:35.690
she asked me to steal some
information from a certain person.

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:39.200
Who did you steal it from?

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:42.200
I don't know his name. It was some boy.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.200
<i>It's definitely Tomoki.</i>

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.790
<i>Souma first made him deliver her messages to me,</i>

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:49.540
<i>and made Hitsuuchi steal those memories from him.</i>

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:52.540
I remembered everything looking at the picture.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:54.800
She mentioned the location of the car crash,

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:57.090
and the supermarket from the second case.

00:10:57.420 --> 00:11:00.890
<i>So everything Souma Sumire
said in her messages to me</i>

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:03.350
<i>was actually from two years ago.</i>

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:06.140
Is there anything else you remember?

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:07.850
Only one more thing.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:09.060
And that is?

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:12.690
I think she was talking about a shower.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.110
<i>A shower?</i>

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:15.440
Kei,

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.320
can you answer me?

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:21.450
How could she be involved in the current events?

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:24.780
I don't know anything.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:29.750
I can't bring myself to imagine you
being friends with a perfectly normal girl.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:32.000
That's mean.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.290
Well, she was a strange girl.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:39.590
Very smart, full of confidence,

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:41.800
but somehow lonely.

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:43.140
And...

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.770
I'm sorry.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:51.060
I don't really want to talk about her.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:54.940
No, I'm sorry for asking. See you.

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:01.570
Souma... You...

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.410
<i>Was such a stupid reason really worth</i>

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:06.200
<i>dying for?</i>

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:08.330
Well, Kei.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.700
It's time for the next request.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.710
Can I ask something?

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:16.750
What is it?

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:20.970
Would you prepare an
Ashiharabashi High uniform for me?

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:24.050
If possible, also textbooks and a gym uniform.

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:28.560
Once our plan succeeds, all information
about abilities will disappear from Sakurada.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:32.890
Our memories will be rewritten,
and I'm sure I'll become a normal student.

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:34.940
We've already arranged for that.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:38.320
It's one of the reasons Tsushima
Shintarou is cooperating with us.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:40.780
I see. Thank you.

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:48.030
We're here. It's time to say goodbye.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:53.660
What is it?

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:55.290
Just wondered if you'd get upset.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.540
That's a lie.

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.550
You knew the result.

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:03.470
I guess. Let me correct myself:
I was trying to make you upset.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:06.800
And what was the point?

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:09.050
Let's drop the act and talk honestly here.

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:17.440
What do you want to talk about?

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:21.440
Let's see... What do you think about the Bureau?

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:23.400
The same as people not involved see it.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.950
Calm, cool, collected, and with no compassion at all.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.490
So it's the same when you're inside it.

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:29.490
Unfortunately.

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:35.080
There's really strong, deep-rooted faith towards
the three founders, especially the unnamed system.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:37.920
They think there's no way she could ever be wrong,

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:40.290
which is why the Bureau is always so calm.

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:43.170
But today it was all destroyed.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:46.630
The Witch didn't predict the current events.

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:47.590
That's right.

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:50.890
The very foundation of the Bureau was shaken.

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:52.350
Did he do something?

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:54.350
Most likely.

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:56.850
There's no point trying to figure out that guy.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.770
He's almost like a monster.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:13:59.810
I see.

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:02.110
Well, I think I've mostly figured it out.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.320
Figured what out?

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.070
What he did.

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:11.120
You're also like a monster.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:15.660
It's not very polite to call a girl a monster.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:19.330
So? Were you watching my future just now?

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:22.800
No, I can't see the future anymore.

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:23.500
Why?

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:27.510
He ordered Oka Eri to use her ability on me.

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:31.140
I've forgotten how to use my clairvoyance.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:32.390
When?

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:33.760
Just a moment ago.

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:37.640
I guess it means my ability served its purpose.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:41.440
Do you think what he's doing is right?

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:43.690
There's no way it could be right.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:46.650
I wouldn't have thought he'd actually
cause an accident on purpose.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:49.700
Then why are you obeying him?

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:52.950
I can't imagine abilities being for the best.

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:57.660
But I don't know how to erase them from this town.

00:14:57.660 --> 00:14:59.580
So I have no choice but to help him.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:02.170
Why do you think abilities are harmful?

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.500
I wonder.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:07.460
Maybe it's because I'm in the Bureau.

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:10.680
You're surely not a monster.

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:14.430
That much should be obvious.
I'm an ordinary government worker.

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:17.520
I'm glad we were able to talk.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:18.310
Thanks.

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:20.940
Goodbye, Souma Sumire.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:22.980
Don't call me by that name.

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:25.520
I'm the Witch.

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:29.490
Tuesday
October 24th

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:34.490
Kei, here's my third instruction for you.

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:36.790
In the morning of October 24th,

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:41.210
you should deliver a book you like to Haruki Misora.

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:43.380
Put a nice cover on it.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:45.380
I'm sure she'll like that.

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:53.550
Kei.

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:57.310
Good morning, Kei.

00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:58.680
Morning.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:02.190
I saw you from the window.

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:05.150
Did you need anything?

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:07.270
I had something to give you.

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:10.780
I put it into the mailbox, so take a look later.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:14.240
I could have invited you inside.

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:16.740
I didn't want to impose this early in the morning.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.910
Kei, are you tired?

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:23.920
Yeah.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.250
It's a bit painful.

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:32.760
You should rest then.

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:36.430
There's just a few more things that I have to do.

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:37.510
No.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:38.640
No?

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:40.770
What you have to do is rest.

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:43.230
It's fine.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.690
I'm good at pushing myself.

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:48.690
It's the first time I ever heard
the word "painful" from you.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:52.900
Even two years ago, when Souma Sumire died,

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.700
you never said such a thing.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:00.950
What happened?

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:02.250
Nothing really.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:05.920
I've simply been thinking about something.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.420
And what is this something?

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:11.260
It's basically about Souma.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:13.420
Did you figure something out?

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:16.220
Yeah, I think I've worked out most of it.

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:19.220
It's just like you said yesterday.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:20.680
No matter the reason,

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:23.230
there's no way dying was the right thing to do.

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:29.730
Souma Sumire died for your sake, didn't she?

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:36.740
You really should rest.

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:39.740
You should lie down and stop thinking about things.

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:43.200
Thanks.

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:45.830
I'm fine, though.

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:48.710
What are you going to do now?

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:52.090
I'll aim for the happiest ending.

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:56.680
I can't do anything to help you, then.

00:17:57.340 --> 00:18:00.470
And since I can't help you, I'll be waiting for you.

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:05.310
Thanks. I'll do my best.

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:27.370
<i>The world inside Katagiri Honoka's dream...</i>

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:33.380
Tyltyl? Mytyl?

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:42.180
<i>They're locked.</i>

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:44.390
<i>It's that Bureau employee's ability.</i>

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:57.820
Tyltyl?

00:18:57.820 --> 00:19:00.240
No, I'm not Tyltyl.

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:02.030
I'm an ordinary bird.

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:04.790
Ordinary birds don't talk.

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:07.250
I'm a bird that talks, then.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:10.250
I don't have any god-like powers.

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:13.500
Was it Tyltyl or Mytyl that created you?

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:14.840
Tyltyl.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:18.260
I was born right before his time was stopped.

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:20.130
What happened?

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:22.340
First, Mytyl's time was stopped.

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:25.850
The Bureau people came soon after that.

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:27.350
<i>I see...</i>

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:30.730
<i>They locked Katagiri Honoka in reality,</i>

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:33.440
<i>and then entered the dream world.</i>

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:36.900
Tyltyl can't oppose the Bureau.

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:40.450
He can't do anything when
they use Mytyl as a shield.

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:43.450
What did they do?

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:47.660
They asked Tyltyl if he knows a future-seer.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:51.540
And Tyltyl told them about Sumire,
just like they asked him to.

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:55.250
Why didn't Tyltyl create himself?

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:58.300
He was planning to.

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:01.260
But you know, Index asked him a few questions.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:06.510
"Is there anyone in this world other
than you two who has god-like powers?"

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:10.640
"Are you trying to create one right now?"

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:14.400
And he had no choice but to answer them honestly.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:15.270
Yeah.

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:19.030
"I was trying to clone myself, but decided not to."

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:22.030
I don't know what's happening in reality,

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:24.570
but please, help Mytyl.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:26.030
Answer my questions, then.

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:28.910
When did the Bureau people appear here?

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:31.290
Around three weeks ago.

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:34.540
Did they leave the dream world immediately?

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:38.340
No, they went to meet with Sumire from this world.

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:42.130
They talked with her, and then stopped her time.

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:45.430
Do you know what they talked about?

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:46.930
No, I don't.

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:50.680
I was just watching them from high above.

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:53.350
I see.

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:56.480
By the Bureau people,
you meant Index, Kagaya, and...

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:58.860
the man who always smiles?

00:20:58.860 --> 00:20:59.440
Yeah.

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:03.450
The last one is called Urachi Masamune.

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:05.450
<i>Urachi?</i>

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:07.200
Something wrong?

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:08.410
It's nothing.

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:12.580
Anyway, once you're back in reality,
I want you to contact Sumire.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.960
I'm sure she'll do something.

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:17.420
Okay, I'll try to do that.

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:23.630
But I don't know how to contact Souma myself...

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:33.350
The rain woke me up...

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:38.190
<i>Urachi?</i>

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:42.980
<i>That name was in volume 407 of the Script...</i>

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:45.070
<i>During the first year of Sakurada,</i>

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:48.660
<i>two of the first three ability users</i>

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:51.490
<i>were Urachi Seijurou and Urachi Haruko.</i>

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:55.000
<i>The Urachis...</i>

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:56.500
Next Episode

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:58.210
Is the restriction of abilities progressing?

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:00.000
I'm scared of abilities.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.380
I can't make a decision yet.

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:02.920
Mr. Tsushima! Why?

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:04.880
I... I want to stay selfish.

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:06.590
What will Urachi Masamune do next?

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:08.890
I want to like this town.

00:22:16.430 --> 00:22:20.400
On such a cold dark sky of grey

00:22:22.690 --> 00:22:26.610
Rises the sun, which breathes life into it

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:32.870
A scenery so plain and so mundane

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:42.460
And yet it seems to break my heart, it's so dear to me

00:22:43.340 --> 00:22:46.920
As the time never stops passing by

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:49.300
You get lost while searching for

00:22:49.300 --> 00:22:53.180
Pure like the rays of a morning star

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:56.100
What we all yearn for the most

00:22:56.100 --> 00:22:59.060
In what colors bliss is dyed

00:22:59.060 --> 00:22:59.520
In what colors bliss is dyed

00:22:59.640 --> 00:23:02.150
Struggling against all your past mistakes

00:23:02.150 --> 00:23:05.190
At last from the answer you found kindness fills your heart

00:23:05.780 --> 00:23:06.480
More beautiful than anything you know

00:23:06.480 --> 00:23:08.360
More beautiful than anything you know

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:11.990
And you find it behind a dark veil of sadness

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:14.490
If I closed my eyes and stopped my thoughts

00:23:14.490 --> 00:23:16.240
If it were so simple to just

00:23:16.240 --> 00:23:19.250
Lock your own heart

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:22.380
How lovely life would be

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:27.630
But I believe you have the key

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:33.970
To let my soul be free
